-- title:
--   Uniqueness of rigidified pairs over a connected base
-- statement:
--   The theorem is stated inside a very large package of data; the hypotheses fall into the groups listed below, each named, and the conclusion is then stated in full.
--
--   **Base arithmetic data.** Primes $r$ and $\bar r$ with $\bar r \ne r$ (`hrr`), a nonzero natural number $N$ with $r \nmid N$ (`hrN`), $\bar r \nmid N$ (`hrbarN`) and $N$ squarefree (`hN`). A characteristic-zero domain $\mathcal O$ which is a discrete valuation ring (`hdvr`), an irreducible element $\pi$ (`hπ`), $\mathcal O$ being $\pi$-adically complete (`hcomplete`), with residue ring of cardinality $r$ (`hres`) and $(r) = (\pi)$ in $\mathcal O$ (`hunr`); $K_0$ a characteristic-zero fraction field of $\mathcal O$. A characteristic-zero domain $\mathit{Onr}$ over $\mathcal O$ with an $\mathcal O$-algebra automorphism $F_r$, complete for the ideal generated by $\pi$ (`hOnr_complete`), that ideal being maximal (`hOnr_max`), every element of $\mathit{Onr}$ satisfying a monic polynomial over $\mathcal O$ modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_alg`), every monic polynomial of positive degree over $\mathit{Onr}$ having a root modulo $\pi$ (`hOnr_closed`), and $F_r(x) \equiv x^r \pmod \pi$ (`hFr`). A monoid homomorphism $\mathrm{vdet} : \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0) \to \mathbb Z$ (written multiplicatively) with $\mathrm{vdet}(g) = n$ if and only if $\det g = u\pi^{n}$ for some unit $u$ of $\mathcal O$ (`hvdet`). Finally $2$ is a unit of $\mathcal O$ (`h2`).
--
--   **Indefinite side and moduli.** Rationals $a,b$ such that $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a,b]$ is indefinite ($0<a$ or $0<b$) and is a division algebra at exactly the finite places above $r$ and $\bar r$ (`hB`), together with a maximal order $\Lambda$ (`hΛ`) containing all rational integers (`hΛℤ`). A scheme $\mathcal X$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with a point map $\mathrm{pt}$ assigning to each fake elliptic curve with $\Lambda$-action and level-$N$ structure over a ring $S$ a point of $\mathcal X$ over the given base map, such that $(\mathcal X,f,\mathrm{pt})$ is a coarse moduli space (`h𝒳`: invariance under isomorphism, compatibility with pullbacks, bijectivity on geometric points over algebraically closed fields, and the universal property). An auxiliary level $n$ with $3 \le n$, $r \nmid n$, $\bar r \nmid n$ and $n$ coprime to $N$, a scheme $M$ over $\operatorname{Spec}\mathcal O$ with point map $\mathrm{ptF}$ for curves with full level-$n$ structure which is a fine moduli space (`hM`), and a group $G$ acting by $\rho : G \to \operatorname{Aut} M$ with labels $\chi : G \to \Lambda$ realising the twisting of level structures (`hρ`). A map $p : M \to \mathcal X$ over the base (`hp`), invariant under $\rho$ (`hρp`) and compatible with the two point maps (`hp_pt`). For each prime $\ell \ne r,\bar r$ a coarse moduli scheme $\mathcal Y_\ell$ for curves with extra level-$\ell$ structure (`h𝒴`) together with two degeneracy maps $d_0,d_1 : \mathcal Y_\ell \to \mathcal X$ over the base (`hd₀f`, `hd₁f`), $d_0$ forgetting the extra structure (`hd₀`) and $d_1$ recording the quotient by a level-$\ell$ isogeny (`hd₁`). Atkin–Lehner maps $a_r, a_{\bar r} : \mathcal X \to \mathcal X$ over the base (`harf`, `harbarf`) computing the Atkin–Lehner quotients at $r$ and at $\bar r$ on points (`har`, `harbar`).
--
--   **Definite side.** Rationals $a_1,b_1$ with $\mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1]$ definite and ramified exactly at $\bar r$ (`hdef`), a maximal order $\Lambda_1$ (`hΛ₁`), an Eichler order $R_1$ of level $N$ (`hR₁`) contained in $\Lambda_1$ (`hRΛ₁`), an idele $n_1$ in the prime Hecke set of $R_1$ at $r$ (`hn₁`) such that the intersection order $R_1 \cap n_1 R_1 n_1^{-1}$ is Eichler of level $Nr$ (`hS₁`), an injective $\mathbb Q$-algebra embedding $\iota_0 : \mathbb H[\mathbb Q,a_1,b_1] \to M_2(K_0)$ (`hι₀`), and a height-one prime $v$ of $\mathbb Z$ containing $r$ (`hv`). A subgroup $\Gamma_t$ of the unit group which coincides with the group of units integral at all places $w \ne v$ (`hΓt`), elements $s(\ell)$ and ideles $sf(\ell)$ for each prime $\ell \ne r,\bar r$ satisfying the four conditions of `hs` (agreement of $sf(\ell)$ with $s(\ell)$ away from $r$, triviality at $r$, membership of the relevant Hecke set according as $\ell \mid N$ or not, and $\mathrm{nrd}(s(\ell)) = \ell$), the groups $\Gamma_{t,\ell} = \Gamma_t \cap s(\ell)\Gamma_t s(\ell)^{-1}$ (`hΓtℓ`), and a unit $\bar w$ of reduced norm $\bar r$ normalising $\Gamma_t$ (`hwbar`). A coordinate map $\mathrm{coord} : \Lambda \to \mathbb Z_{p^2}(r)^2$ which is an order coordinate in the sense of `IsOrderCoord` (additive, sending $1$ to $(1,0)$, multiplicative for the twisted law, injective, with dense image and the prescribed trace identity) (`hcoord`).
--
--   **The distinguished object over the residue field.** Over $k_0 := \mathit{Onr}/(\pi)$: a fake elliptic curve $A_0$, a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $X_0$ of height $4$ (`hX₀`), formal coordinates $\theta_0$ in two variables for $A_0$, and the identification of $A_0$ as a formal module via $\mathrm{coord}$, $X_0$, $\theta_0$ (`hA₀`). Endomorphisms $e(\gamma), e'(\gamma)$ of $A_0$ for $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$, with $e(\gamma)$ over the base (`he`) and degrees $\deg(\gamma)$, subject to: $(e(\gamma), e'(\gamma))$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{\deg \gamma}$ and $e(\gamma)$ preserves the level structure (`hE1`); multiplicativity of $\gamma \mapsto e(\gamma)$ up to powers of $r$ (`hE1mul`); $e(\gamma) = [c]$ up to powers of $r$ when $\gamma$ is the integer scalar $c$ (`hE1sc`); conversely, $\gamma$ is a rational scalar whenever $e(\gamma)$ is a positive integer multiplication up to a power of $r$ (`hE1'`). The matrix normalisation `hE2`: for every injective ring homomorphism from the centraliser of the $X_0$-action (the range of $X_0.\mathrm{actEnd}$ together with $X_0.\mathrm{varpiEnd}$) into $M_2(K_0)$ there is $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ such that each $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$ admits an element $\varepsilon$ of that centraliser and an integer $k_\gamma$ with $\varepsilon$ inducing $e(\gamma)$ on nilpotent formal points and with image $r^{k_\gamma} g\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g^{-1}$. The labelling hypothesis `hE3`: each full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$ admits $\mathrm{lab} : \Gamma_t \to \Lambda$ with $e(\gamma)$ acting on $P_0$ as $\mathrm{lab}(\gamma)$, multiplicative modulo $n$ and compatible with integer scalars modulo $n$. The exhaustion hypothesis `hE4`: over an algebraically closed field $k$ over $k_0$, every level-preserving isogeny pair of $r$-power degree on a curve pulled back from $A_0$ comes, up to powers of $r$, from some $e(\gamma)$. The order-action hypotheses `hE5a`–`hE5e`: an order $R_2 \le R_1$ (`hR₂`, `hR₂o`) with $r$-power denominators relative to $R_1$ (`hR₂r`), endomorphisms $\hat e(x)$ of $A_0$ over the base for $x \in R_2$ (`hê`), which are homomorphisms for the group law, commute with the $\Lambda$-action and preserve the level (`hE5a`), send $1$ to the identity (`hE5b1`), are multiplicative (`hE5b2`), send integers to the corresponding multiplications (`hE5b3`), satisfy $\hat e(\bar x)\hat e(x) = [\mathrm{nrd}\,x]$ (`hE5c`), agree with $e(\gamma)$ up to powers of $r$ when $x = r^k\gamma$ (`hE5d`), and admit a single matrix normalisation valid simultaneously for $\Gamma_t$ and for $R_2$ (`hE5e`).
--
--   **Formal-module and Drinfeld-space side.** A ring homomorphism $\iota : \mathbb Z_{p^2}(r) \to \mathit{Onr}$; a formal $\mathcal O_D$-module $\Phi$ over $\mathit{Onr}/(r)$ which is special for the induced structure map (`hΦ`) and of height $4$ (`hΦ4`); a moduli package $\mathit{MD}$ over $\mathit{Onr}$ which is a Zariski sheaf (`hMD`); a family $\eta$ sending rigidified $\Phi$-data over a ring $B$ with $r$ nilpotent to points of $\mathit{MD}$, with `hη` (three clauses: $\eta$ separates admissible data exactly up to isomorphism, $\eta$ is natural in the base, and $\eta$ is surjective after passage to a Zariski cover by localisations). An injective ring homomorphism $E_0$ from the centraliser of the $\Phi$-action into $M_2(K_0)$ whose image is commensurable with $M_2(\mathcal O)$ in the precise sense of `hE₀` (existence of $m$ with the two stated inclusions after scaling by $r^m$). A family of maps $\mathrm{eD}$ from the point functor $\mathcal G(\mathcal O, \mathit{MD})$ to the product of the functor corepresented by $\mathit{Onr}$ with the Deligne-datum functor $\Omega(K_0,\pi)$, natural in the base (`hnatD`), bijective on each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra in which $\pi$ is nilpotent (`hbijD`), with first component the structure map $\psi$ (`hfstD`), translating the $\mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$-action on moduli points into the twisted action on $\Omega$ (`hGLD`), translating $\pi$-translation into the Frobenius twist of the first component (`hPiD`), and with $\pi$-translates always existing (`hPiexD`). A map $\kappa : \mathit{Onr}/(\pi) \to \mathit{Onr}/(r)$ compatible with the quotient maps (`hκ`), an integer $n_0$ and a series $\beta_0$ exhibiting an isogeny $\Phi \to X_0$ (transported by $\kappa$) of height $4n_0$ (`hβ₀`). A full level-$n$ structure $P_0$ on $A_0$.
--
--   **Atkin–Lehner data at $\bar r$ over the residue field.** A fake elliptic curve $A_{0w}$ over $k_0$ with maps $a_w, a_w', b_w, b_w'$ over the base (`haw`, `haw'`, `hbw`, `habw`) such that $(a_w,a_w')$ realises the Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ (`hALw`), $(b_w,b_w')$ is an isogeny pair of degree $r^{k_w}$ (`hBSw`) with $b_w$ level-preserving (`hBSwlev`), and `hJOINTw`, the joint matrix normalisation asserting that for every injective $E_0$ as above there is a single $g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ normalising all $e(\gamma)$, $\gamma \in \Gamma_t$, as in `hE2` and simultaneously normalising the composite $a_w$ followed by $b_w$ against $\iota_0(\bar w)$.
--
--   **The classifying map $\Xi$.** A family $\Xi$ sending, for each Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ with $\pi$ nilpotent and each $\psi : \mathit{Onr} \to B$, a rigidified curve over $(B,\psi)$ — that is, a fake elliptic curve $E$ over $B$ together with a rigidification consisting of the reduction $E_b$ of $E$ modulo $\pi$, a curve $A_b$ pulled back from $A_0$ along the residue of $\psi$, and an isogeny pair $(\varphi,\varphi')$ of degree $r^{d}$ from $E_b$ to $A_b$ with $\varphi$ level-preserving — to a point of $\mathcal G(\mathcal O,\mathit{MD})$, subject to: `hΞleg`, over a $B$ whose only idempotents are $0$ and $1$ the structure map of $\Xi$ is a Frobenius twist $F_r^{k}$ of $\psi$ for some $k \in \mathbb Z$; `hΞnat`, compatibility with base change along $\varphi : B \to B'$ for pullbacks of rigidified curves; `hΞiso`, invariance of $\Xi$ under an isomorphism of the underlying curves together with the $r$-power correspondence between the rigidifications; and `hΞdef`, over a connected $B$ with $r$ nilpotent, the computation of $\Xi$ through $\eta$: given a formal-module structure $(X,\theta)$ on the curve there exist $j \le 1$ and a rigidified $\Phi$-datum $t$ with $t.X = X$, transported from $\theta_0$, $\kappa$, $\beta_0$ in the sense of `IsRigTransport`, admissible for the $(-j)$-fold Frobenius twist of $\psi$, such that $\Xi$ is the point built from $\eta$ at that twist. Finally an element $g_0 \in \mathrm{GL}_2(K_0)$ together with the two equivariance hypotheses: `heqΓ`, over a connected $B$, if $\varrho'$ is the translate of $\varrho$ by $e(\gamma)$ then $\Xi\langle E,\varrho\rangle$ and $\Xi\langle E,\varrho'\rangle$ are related by the action of $r^{c} \cdot g_0\,\iota_0(\gamma)\,g_0^{-1}$ for some $c \in \mathbb Z$; and `heqW`, over a connected $B$ in which $\bar r$ is invertible, the analogous statement for an Atkin–Lehner quotient at $\bar r$ and the element $\bar w$, the relation between the two rigidifications being the one spelt out there by means of $a_w$ followed by $b_w$.
--
--   **Conclusion.** Write $\psi^{\circ} := F_r^{-\mathrm{vdet}(g_0)}\circ\psi$ for the Frobenius twist of $\psi$ by the negative of the valuation of $\det g_0$. For every Noetherian $\mathcal O$-algebra $B$ in which the image of $\pi$ is nilpotent, whose only idempotents are $0$ and $1$, every $\psi : \mathit{Onr} \to_{\mathcal O} B$, every Deligne datum $P$ over $B$, and every two pairs $(E,\varrho)$ and $(E',\varrho')$ consisting of a fake elliptic curve over $B$ and a rigidification of it relative to $A_0$ with respect to $\psi^{\circ}$, such that the structure map of $\Xi\langle E,\varrho\rangle$ equals $\psi^{\circ}$ and $\mathrm{eD}$ of $\Xi\langle E,\varrho\rangle$ is carried to $(\psi,P)$ by the twisted action of $g_0^{-1}$, and likewise for $(E',\varrho')$, there exist an isomorphism $i : E.A \cong E'.A$ with $i$ followed by $E'.f$ equal to $E.f$ such that
--
--   (i) $i$ is an isomorphism of fake elliptic curves: it is compatible with the group laws on points over arbitrary bases, commutes with the $\Lambda$-actions, and a point factors through the level structure of $E$ if and only if its image factors through that of $E'$;
--
--   (ii) there are a map $i_b : \varrho.E_b.A \to \varrho'.E_b.A$ with $i_b$ followed by $\varrho'.g_b$ equal to $\varrho.g_b$ followed by $i$, and $i_b$ over the base, a map $u_A : \varrho'.A_b.A \to \varrho.A_b.A$ exhibiting $\varrho'.A_b$ as the pullback of $\varrho.A_b$ along the identity of the base ring and satisfying $u_A$ followed by $\varrho.g_A$ equal to $\varrho'.g_A$, and natural numbers $i_1, j_1$ such that
--   $$i_b \;\text{followed by}\; \varrho'.\varphi,\; u_A,\; \varrho.A_b.\mathrm{act}[r^{i_1}] \;=\; \varrho.\varphi \;\text{followed by}\; \varrho.A_b.\mathrm{act}[r^{j_1}].$$
--
--   This is the uniqueness half of the Čerednik–Drinfeld comparison between rigidified fake elliptic curves in the supersingular stratum and points of the formal upper half-plane: over a connected Noetherian base with $\pi$ nilpotent, two rigidified pairs with the same image under the classifying map $\Xi$ followed by the Drinfeld identification $\mathrm{eD}$, twisted by $g_0^{-1}$, differ by an isomorphism of fake elliptic curves matching the rigidifications up to powers of $r$. The present edition carries the additional hypothesis that $2$ is invertible in $\mathcal O$; it is used by [`CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.evenRigidifiedPair_exists_unique_pullback_lift_of_rigidifiedToG_conn_h2`](thm.html#CerednikDrinfeld.QM.FakeEllipticCurve.evenRigidifiedPair_exists_unique_pullback_lift_of_rigidifiedToG_conn_h2), which combines it with the corresponding existence statement.
